-- א.2: maternity leave under §6 of the Women's Work Law, 1954, within
-- 1.7.2010–1.11.2010 ("the determining period") does not break the
-- employment's continuity: she has the grant with the first salary after
-- her return, or the next at the latest; ¶2: the leave is 26 weeks as a
-- rule, unless §6 lengthens it (outside the corpus); ¶3: not for unpaid
-- leave, or absence treated as one, after the maternity leave: ב governs
-- that. א.3: the circular's other conditions apply to her; ¶2: and to a man
-- who took maternity leave under that law.
@ref akn:att_2__att_2__hc_1__para_5__subpara_a__cls_2 akn:att_2__att_2__hc_1__para_5__subpara_a__cls_2/p2 akn:att_2__att_2__hc_1__para_5__subpara_a__cls_2/p3 akn:att_2__att_2__hc_1__para_5__subpara_a__cls_3 akn:att_2__att_2__hc_1__para_5__subpara_a__cls_3/p2
`maternity leave breaks the grant's continuity` MEANS FALSE
`the maternity leave's length as a rule, in weeks` MEANS 26

`why the Women's Work Law is not here` MEANS
    `outside the corpus` "חוק עבודת נשים, התשי\"ד-1954, סעיף 6"

-- ב: an employee on unpaid leave, or absent as on one, for all or part of
-- the determining period: (1) one entitled to salary for 4 full months
-- and a day more, continuously, in 1.7.2010–31.12.2011, full-time or
-- part-time, has the grant; (2) his position for it is his average over
-- the time he was employed in 1.11.2009–31.10.2010, and if he had no
-- salary at all then, over the time he had salary in 1.11.2010–31.12.2011,
-- continuous or not; (3) paid with the salary of January 2012, by
-- February 2012's at the latest.
@ref akn:att_2__att_2__hc_1__para_5__subpara_b/p2 akn:att_2__att_2__hc_1__para_5__subpara_b__cls_1 akn:att_2__att_2__hc_1__para_5__subpara_b__cls_2 akn:att_2__att_2__hc_1__para_5__subpara_b__cls_2/p2 akn:att_2__att_2__hc_1__para_5__subpara_b__cls_2/p3 akn:att_2__att_2__hc_1__para_5__subpara_b__cls_3
GIVEN `whole months of salary in a row, from 1.7.2010 to 31.12.2011` IS A NUMBER
      `days more beyond them` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `one on unpaid leave has the grant` `whole months of salary in a row, from 1.7.2010 to 31.12.2011` `days more beyond them` IF
        `whole months of salary in a row, from 1.7.2010 to 31.12.2011` AT LEAST 5
    OR (`whole months of salary in a row, from 1.7.2010 to 31.12.2011` AT LEAST 4 AND `days more beyond them` AT LEAST 1)

`the latest salary month one on unpaid leave is paid the grant with` MEANS LIST 2012, 2

