§§ `נספח ד' — טבלת הגדלת המשכורת הקובעת`

-- The table by the month of retirement from the service, January 2009 to
-- December 2012: the rise of columns A, B and C (§14.1.3). Two cells of
-- column C, September and October 2011, print a digit the corpus marks
-- illegible ("0.[לא קריא]338%", "0.77[לא קריא]5%"): they are not read.
@ref akn:att_4__hc_1/t1
@desc A row of annex ד''s table: the month of retirement and the rise of each column.
DECLARE `annex ד' row` HAS
    `the year of retirement`  IS A NUMBER
    `the month of retirement` IS A NUMBER
    `column A`                IS A NUMBER
    `column B`                IS A NUMBER
    `column C`                IS A MAYBE NUMBER

`why two cells of annex ד' are not here` MEANS
    `the text is missing` "נספח ד', עמודה C, ספטמבר-11 ואוקטובר-11: ספרה אחת בכל תא מסומנת [לא קריא]"

`the rows of annex ד'` MEANS
    LIST (`annex ד' row` OF 2009, 1, 0.1488%, 0%, JUST (0%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2009, 2, 0.2976%, 0%, JUST (0%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2009, 3, 0.4464%, 0%, JUST (0%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2009, 4, 0.5952%, 0%, JUST (0%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2009, 5, 0.7440%, 0%, JUST (0%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2009, 6, 0.8929%, 0%, JUST (0%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2009, 7, 1.0417%, 0%, JUST (0%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2009, 8, 1.1905%, 0%, JUST (0%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2009, 9, 1.3393%, 0%, JUST (0%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2009, 10, 1.4881%, 0%, JUST (0%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2009, 11, 1.6369%, 0%, JUST (0%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2009, 12, 1.7857%, 0%, JUST (0%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2010, 1, 1.9345%, 0%, JUST (0%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2010, 2, 2.0833%, 0%, JUST (0%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2010, 3, 2.2321%, 0%, JUST (0%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2010, 4, 2.2500%, 0.1281%, JUST (0%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2010, 5, 2.2500%, 0.2736%, JUST (0%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2010, 6, 2.2500%, 0.4191%, JUST (0%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2010, 7, 2.2500%, 0.5647%, JUST (0%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2010, 8, 2.2500%, 0.7102%, JUST (0%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2010, 9, 2.2500%, 0.8557%, JUST (0%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2010, 10, 2.2500%, 1.0013%, JUST (0%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2010, 11, 2.2500%, 1.1468%, JUST (0%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2010, 12, 2.2500%, 1.2924%, JUST (0%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2011, 1, 0%, 1.4379%, JUST (0%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2011, 2, 0%, 1.5834%, JUST (0%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2011, 3, 0%, 1.7290%, JUST (0%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2011, 4, 0%, 1.8745%, JUST (0%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2011, 5, 0%, 1.9559%, JUST (0.0628%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2011, 6, 0%, 1.9559%, JUST (0.2055%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2011, 7, 0%, 1.9559%, JUST (0.3483%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2011, 8, 0%, 1.9559%, JUST (0.4910%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2011, 9, 0%, 1.9559%, NOTHING),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2011, 10, 0%, 1.9559%, NOTHING),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2011, 11, 0%, 1.9559%, JUST (0.9193%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2011, 12, 0%, 1.9559%, JUST (1.0620%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2012, 1, 0%, 0%, JUST (1.2048%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2012, 2, 0%, 0%, JUST (1.3475%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2012, 3, 0%, 0%, JUST (1.4902%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2012, 4, 0%, 0%, JUST (1.6330%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2012, 5, 0%, 0%, JUST (1.7757%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2012, 6, 0%, 0%, JUST (1.9185%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2012, 7, 0%, 0%, JUST (1.9185%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2012, 8, 0%, 0%, JUST (1.9185%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2012, 9, 0%, 0%, JUST (1.9185%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2012, 10, 0%, 0%, JUST (1.9185%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2012, 11, 0%, 0%, JUST (1.9185%)),
         (`annex ד' row` OF 2012, 12, 0%, 0%, JUST (1.9185%))

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `annex ד' row`
DECIDE `the annex ד' row for` y m IS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `the year of retirement` EQUALS y AND r's `the month of retirement` EQUALS m) `the rows of annex ד'`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
    WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST r

§§ `illustrations`

-- §3: a nurse of a signing employer; a jurist linked to a judicial
-- officer's pay, outside but for §§11, 12 and 16; a teaching employee
-- outside; none of ¶4's scales is in annex א'.
`a nurse of the State` MEANS `2011 framework employee` WITH
    `employed by an employer that signed the 2011 framework agreement` IS TRUE
    `the scale his pay is computed by` IS "אחים ואחיות"
    `his pay is linked to a judicial officer's` IS FALSE
`a jurist linked to a judge's pay` MEANS `2011 framework employee` WITH
    `employed by an employer that signed the 2011 framework agreement` IS TRUE
    `the scale his pay is computed by` IS "משפטנים"
    `his pay is linked to a judicial officer's` IS TRUE
`a teaching employee of the State` MEANS `2011 framework employee` WITH
    `employed by an employer that signed the 2011 framework agreement` IS TRUE
    `the scale his pay is computed by` IS "עובדי הוראה"
    `his pay is linked to a judicial officer's` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `the 2011 framework agreement covers` `a nurse of the State`
#ASSERT NOT `the 2011 framework agreement covers` `a jurist linked to a judge's pay`
#ASSERT `a section of the 2011 framework reaches` 11 `a jurist linked to a judge's pay`
#ASSERT NOT `a section of the 2011 framework reaches` 9 `a jurist linked to a judge's pay`
#ASSERT NOT `the 2011 framework agreement covers` `a teaching employee of the State`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN s YIELD NOT elem s `the scales annex א' of the 2011 framework lists`) `the scales §3 of the 2011 framework keeps out`
#ASSERT count `the scales annex א' of the 2011 framework lists` EQUALS 24
#ASSERT count `the scales the one-time grant reaches in the State's service` EQUALS 22

-- §§4–5: the frame of the three and a half years is the 6.25% §5 reaches
-- in 2013; a body outside amendment 50 has no 2009 frame and no 2012
-- step.
#ASSERT `the 2011 framework cost frame in all` EQUALS 6.25%
#ASSERT `the 2011 framework cost frame for` 2009 FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the 2011 framework allocation on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2013) TRUE EQUALS 6.25%
#ASSERT `the 2011 framework allocation on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2012) FALSE EQUALS 2.25%
#ASSERT `the 2011 framework allocation on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2010) TRUE EQUALS 0

-- §6: a 2010 overtime payment is in the base; an expense reimbursement and
-- a top-up to the minimum wage are not; the base is 2010's average.
`overtime of 2010` MEANS `2011 framework pay component` WITH
    `its kind` IS `overtime, shifts, duty, standby, call-outs or incentive pay`
    `paid monthly, weekly or daily` IS TRUE
    `updated by the cost-of-living agreements` IS FALSE
    `a minimum-wage top-up` IS FALSE
    `paid in 2010` IS TRUE
    `counted for the hour value` IS FALSE
    `bound to the hour value or the pension salary` IS TRUE
`a minimum-wage top-up of 2010` MEANS `2011 framework pay component` WITH
    `its kind` IS `another supplement`
    `paid monthly, weekly or daily` IS TRUE
    `updated by the cost-of-living agreements` IS TRUE
    `a minimum-wage top-up` IS TRUE
    `paid in 2010` IS TRUE
    `counted for the hour value` IS FALSE
    `bound to the hour value or the pension salary` IS FALSE
`a fixed shekel supplement outside the hour value` MEANS `2011 framework pay component` WITH
    `its kind` IS `another supplement`
    `paid monthly, weekly or daily` IS TRUE
    `updated by the cost-of-living agreements` IS TRUE
    `a minimum-wage top-up` IS FALSE
    `paid in 2010` IS TRUE
    `counted for the hour value` IS FALSE
    `bound to the hour value or the pension salary` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `in the base of the 2011 framework cost frame` `overtime of 2010`
#ASSERT NOT `in the base of the 2011 framework cost frame` `a minimum-wage top-up of 2010`
#ASSERT NOT `in the base of the 2011 supplement` `a fixed shekel supplement outside the hour value`
#ASSERT `§9.8 raises` `a fixed shekel supplement outside the hour value`
#ASSERT NOT `§9.8 raises` `overtime of 2010`
#ASSERT `a supplement under §9.8 on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2011) `a fixed shekel supplement outside the hour value` 400 EQUALS 409
#ASSERT `the 2011 framework salary base from` (LIST 9000, 9000, 9000, 9000, 9000, 9000, 11000, 11000, 11000, 11000, 11000, 11000) EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `the employer §7 computes the cost for` `a university` EQUALS "האוניברסיטאות"
#ASSERT NOT `a 2011 framework supplement counts for the minimum-wage top-up` FALSE

-- §9: 2.25% of 10,000 in 2011; 4.25% from 2012 where no agreement came by
-- 30.11.2011; 6.25% from 2013 where neither did; 4.25% in 2013 where only
-- the first did. תוספת 2001 on a base of 9,000 at 3.6%.
#ASSERT `תוספת 2011 on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2011) 10000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 225
#ASSERT `תוספת 2011 on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2012) 10000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 425
#ASSERT `תוספת 2011 on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2013) 10000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 625
#ASSERT `תוספת 2011 on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2013) 10000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS 425
#ASSERT `תוספת 2011 on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2013) 10000 TRUE TRUE EQUALS 225
#ASSERT `תוספת 2011 on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2010) 10000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `תוספת 2001 in §9.3's order` 9000 `the rate of תוספת 2001 by the agreement of 31.1.01` 500 EQUALS 324
#ASSERT `תוספת 2011 counts for` `pensions and the determining salary`
#ASSERT NOT `תוספת 2011 counts for` `the 2011 supplement's minimum-wage top-up`
-- §10.3–10.4 by default reach §5's allocation for a body under amendment 50
#ASSERT `the 2011 supplement's rate on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2013) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the 2011 framework allocation on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2013) TRUE
#ASSERT `the share of their table a special scale is paid on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2012) EQUALS 104.25%
#ASSERT NOT `a §10 agreement may pay for work done on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2010)

-- §11: 300 and 200; a third child adds nothing; 2% more in the index.
#ASSERT `the 2011 framework day-care supplement for` 3 300 200 EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `a 2011 framework day-care amount updated each January` 300 (LIST 100, 102) EQUALS 306
#ASSERT `entitled to the 2011 framework day-care supplement for the child` TRUE 4
#ASSERT NOT `entitled to the 2011 framework day-care supplement for the child` TRUE 5
#ASSERT `a general arrangement the 2011 framework keeps` TRUE 350 550
#ASSERT NOT `a general arrangement the 2011 framework keeps` TRUE 350 500
#ASSERT `an older child's day-care arrangement goes on under the 2011 framework` 6

-- §12.2(א)(1): 6% and 5% become 6.5% and 5.5% in 2011, 7% and 6% in 2013;
-- a deduction of 5.8% goes to 6%; a rate above the cap stays.
`6% and 5%` MEANS `2011 framework fund rates` WITH `the employer's for benefits` IS 6%, `the employee's deduction` IS 5%
#ASSERT (`the rates in a new accrual pension fund under §12.2 on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2011) `6% and 5%`)'s `the employer's for benefits` EQUALS 6.5%
#ASSERT (`the rates in a new accrual pension fund under §12.2 on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2011) `6% and 5%`)'s `the employee's deduction` EQUALS 5.5%
#ASSERT (`the rates in a new accrual pension fund under §12.2 on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2013) `6% and 5%`)'s `the employer's for benefits` EQUALS 7%
#ASSERT (`the rates in a new accrual pension fund under §12.2 on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2013) `6% and 5%`)'s `the employee's deduction` EQUALS 6%
#ASSERT `a deduction grown by half a point or to` (5.8%) (6%) EQUALS 6%
#ASSERT `an employer's rate grown by half a point to` (7%) (6.5%) EQUALS 7%
-- (א)(2): 7% and 6.8% become 7.5% and 7% in 2011, and stay there.
`7% and 6.8%` MEANS `2011 framework fund rates` WITH `the employer's for benefits` IS 7%, `the employee's deduction` IS 6.8%
#ASSERT (`the rates in managers' insurance under §12.2 on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2011) `7% and 6.8%`)'s `the employer's for benefits` EQUALS 7.5%
#ASSERT (`the rates in managers' insurance under §12.2 on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2013) `7% and 6.8%`)'s `the employee's deduction` EQUALS 7%
#ASSERT (`the rates in managers' insurance under §12.2 on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2013) `6% and 5%`)'s `the employer's for benefits` EQUALS 7%
#ASSERT (`the rates in managers' insurance under §12.2 on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2010) `6% and 5%`)'s `the employer's for benefits` EQUALS 6%
-- (ב): 5% and 5% become 5.5% and 5.5%, then 6% and 6%.
`5% and 5%` MEANS `2011 framework fund rates` WITH `the employer's for benefits` IS 5%, `the employee's deduction` IS 5%
#ASSERT (`the rates on uninsured components under §12.2(ב) on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2013) `5% and 5%`)'s `the employer's for benefits` EQUALS 6%
#ASSERT (`the rates on uninsured components under §12.2(ב) on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2011) `5% and 5%`)'s `the employee's deduction` EQUALS 5.5%

-- §13: not in the education system.
#ASSERT NOT `may take the first school day as a day of choice` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `may take the first school day as a day of choice` FALSE TRUE

-- §14: retired in June 2010, 10,000: column A in 2011, B on top in 2012.
#ASSERT `an eligible retiree under §14.1.1` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2010) TRUE
#ASSERT `the determining salary raised under §14 for` 10000 2010 6 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2011) EQUALS JUST 10225
#ASSERT `the determining salary raised under §14 for` 10000 2010 6 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2012) EQUALS JUST (10225 TIMES (1 PLUS 0.4191%))
#ASSERT `the determining salary raised under §14 for` 10000 2010 6 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2010) EQUALS JUST 10000
#ASSERT `the determining salary raised under §14 for` 10000 2011 9 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2013) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the determining salary raised under §14 for` 10000 2011 9 (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2012) EQUALS JUST (10000 TIMES (1 PLUS 1.9559%))
#ASSERT count `the rows of annex ד'` EQUALS 48
#ASSERT `an eligible retiree's jubilee grant under §14.5` 6000 10000 10225 EQUALS 6135
#ASSERT NOT `§14.4's determining salary takes in` `the jubilee grant`

-- Annex ד''s column A against its own arithmetic: each month of 2009 and
-- 2010's first quarter adds a twelfth of 1.7857%, to four places, until
-- the column reaches 5.1.1's 2.25% in April 2010.
GIVEN r IS AN `annex ד' row`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the months from December 2008 to the row` r IS
    (r's `the year of retirement` MINUS 2008) TIMES 12 PLUS r's `the month of retirement` MINUS 12

GIVEN r IS AN `annex ד' row`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the column A a twelfth of 4.1.1's rate a month gives` r IS
    (min (`the months from December 2008 to the row` r TIMES `the 2011 framework cost frame for each of 2009, 2010 and 2011` DIVIDED BY 12) (2.25%)) `to the nearest` 0.000001

GIVEN r IS AN `annex ד' row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the row's column A is a twelfth of 4.1.1's rate a month` r IF
    r's `column A` EQUALS `the column A a twelfth of 4.1.1's rate a month gives` r

`column A is a twelfth of 4.1.1's rate a month, to 2.25%` MEANS
    all `the row's column A is a twelfth of 4.1.1's rate a month` (filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `the year of retirement` AT MOST 2010) `the rows of annex ד'`)
#ASSERT `column A is a twelfth of 4.1.1's rate a month, to 2.25%`

-- §16: none reduced after the bill; 2010's back where 2009's was made.
#ASSERT NOT `§16.1(3) leaves a further havraa reduction possible in` 2011 TRUE
#ASSERT `the 2010 havraa reduction paid back` 800 TRUE EQUALS 800
#ASSERT `the 2010 havraa reduction paid back` 800 FALSE EQUALS 0

-- §18: a claim pending in a court is not exhausted.
#ASSERT `the 2011 framework exhausts the claim` FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2012)
#ASSERT NOT `the 2011 framework exhausts the claim` TRUE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2012)
#ASSERT `the arbitration institution agreement stands on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2014) NOTHING

-- Annex ב': 2,000 at 75%; by the hour, 92.085 hours a month is half a
-- position; one on unpaid leave with 4 months and a day.
#ASSERT `the one-time grant of 2010` TRUE TRUE 0.75 EQUALS 1500
#ASSERT `the one-time grant of 2010` FALSE TRUE 1 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the position of one paid by the hour, for the grant` 92.085 EQUALS 0.5
#ASSERT `the position of one paid by the day, for the grant` 12.5 6 EQUALS 0.5
#ASSERT `one on unpaid leave has the grant` 4 1
#ASSERT NOT `one on unpaid leave has the grant` 4 0

-- Annex ג': 12.5% from 2011 (6.5% and 6%), 13% from 2013 in the accrual
-- pension; at 7% in place of severance, 84% and 16% in place of 72% and
-- 28%, and at 6% the agreement's own 72%.
`13% and 6.5%` MEANS `the alternative arrangement's rates` WITH `the employer's for benefits` IS 7%, `the employer's in place of severance` IS 6%, `the employee's for benefits` IS 6.5%
#ASSERT `the accrual-pension rates under annex ג' on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2013) FALSE EQUALS JUST `13% and 6.5%`
#ASSERT `what annex ג' puts in place of 72%` (7%) EQUALS JUST (84%)
#ASSERT `what annex ג' puts in place of 28%` (7%) EQUALS JUST (16%)
#ASSERT `what annex ג' puts in place of 72%` (6.5%) EQUALS JUST (78%)
#ASSERT `what annex ג' puts in place of 72%` (25 DIVIDED BY 3 DIVIDED BY 100) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (6%) TIMES 12 EQUALS 72%

-- Held to the agreement of 3.3.99 it amends: §12's product at 6% is the
-- 72% of its chapter ח' (1) and the rest its 28% (2); §11's 12.5% and 6%
-- from 2011 raise its chapter ז' §1's 12% and 5.5%; §9's earlier wording
-- of the alternative arrangement (7% to an independent fund, beside 5% and
-- 5%) is its chapter ד' §8; §7's base is its chapter ד' §3(א)'s.
#ASSERT (6%) TIMES 12 EQUALS `the share of severance the contributions take the place of`
#ASSERT 100% MINUS (6%) TIMES 12 EQUALS `the share of severance the employer pays at the end`
#ASSERT 6.5% PLUS 6% GREATER THAN `the employer's accrual contribution under the 1999 agreement`
#ASSERT 6% GREATER THAN `the employee's accrual deduction under the 1999 agreement`
#ASSERT `the alternative arrangement's rate for the self-employed fund` EQUALS 7%
#ASSERT `the employer's provident-fund rate beside the alternative arrangement` EQUALS 5%
#ASSERT `the employee's provident-fund rate beside the alternative arrangement` EQUALS 5%
#ASSERT `in a permanent employee's accrual base` `another salary component`
#ASSERT NOT `in a permanent employee's accrual base` `a tax gross-up`
#ASSERT `annex ג' covers` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2011) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 1999) `a new employee` `another scale` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `annex ג' covers` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2010) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 1999) `a new employee` `another scale` TRUE
#ASSERT `annex ג' brings a permanent employee's component into the pension fund` `another salary component under annex ג'`
#ASSERT NOT `annex ג' brings a permanent employee's component into the pension fund` `a tax gross-up under annex ג'`
#ASSERT `actively insured in managers' insurance under annex ג'` 3

-- F-framework-2011-a's evidence: the alternative arrangement's second
-- step is eleven months after every other step of 2013, and in between it
-- keeps 2011's rates.
`annex ג''s alternative arrangement rises on 1.12.2013` MEANS
        DATE_SERIAL `the day annex ג''s §9(ב) raises the alternative arrangement from` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the day every other step of 2013 is taken` EQUALS 334
    AND `the alternative arrangement's rates under annex ג' on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2013)
            EQUALS `the alternative arrangement's rates under annex ג' on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2011)
#ASSERT `annex ג''s alternative arrangement rises on 1.12.2013`

-- F-framework-2011-c's evidence: §14.4 names no section of the Pensions
-- Law.
`§14.4 names no section of the Pensions Law` MEANS
    `the section of the Pensions Law §14.4 names` EQUALS ""
#ASSERT `§14.4 names no section of the Pensions Law`
